  "verdict": "CENTRE SHIFT IS DETECTABLE IN RANK: valid-vs-BCN image AUROC 0.9657 -- bank similarity sees the cross-centre shift that N3 showed head margins cannot (margins move the WRONG way; this score moves the right way). At the registered valid-p1 operating point (kept deliberately conservative so ~99% of in-domain images pass), 46.4% of BCN images fall below threshold and are auto-downgraded to the single-view report. The upper tail of the BCN score distribution overlaps the in-domain distribution, so the conservative threshold converts strong rank separation into a partial gate: the closest-to-domain BCN images pass. The gate materially NARROWS the N3 boundary for centre shift; it does not close it, and the paper should quote both numbers rather than the AUROC alone. Gross non-dermoscopic inputs: 3/5 sanity probes flagged; the fully synthetic probes (no dermoscopic content) were ALL flagged, so the gate does catch inputs that are not dermoscopy at all. Spill on legitimate in-domain images: 1.27% of Derm7pt TEST flagged (valid, the fitting population, 1.48% by construction)."
